arliest-sclk usable frame.","Skyline traced per frame with the SAME settings as the single-frame tests (sigma 1.5 px, threshold 4.0, 5-px median smoothing, >12 px running-median outlier rejection); not tuned. Each frame's columns are converted to true azimuth/elevation with its own CAHVORE model and the waypoint attitude, binned to 2-deg cells (>= 10 traced columns, median elevation); frames are merged per cell by median. Cells with no frame or no accepted trace are NaN (null) and are not scored.","Rover-hardware rule: no azimuth sector is masked. On the development frames the rover deck/RTG appears only in the lowest part of the frame, well below the skyline, so the geometric rule is: nothing masked. Not examined for held-out frames before the run.","Matching: heading known to +-10 deg (11 shifts of 2 deg); one elevation offset per candidate (clipped to +-0.5 deg); terrain closer than 150 m is not used to form the predicted horizon (CTX samples >= 150 m and MOLA only) but every traced azimuth is scored for every candidate (v2; v1 excluded such azimuths per candidate, see README 8b); score = RMS over all valid azimuths. The same near-field and offset rules are used in all four ablation rows; only the frame set and the backdrop change. A candidate must score at least 20 azimuths AND 50% of the valid azimuths: this guard was added after the first development run, in which the single-frame best candidate scored only 20 of 48 azimuths because the near-field rule dropped the rest (a degenerate 'win'). It was not tuned on position error.","Horizon = max over CTX samples (40 m, to 15 km) and MOLA samples (250 m, to 120 km, only outside the CTX footprint or beyond 15 km), Mars curvature term, eye 2 m above the CTX elevation at the candidate. CTX minus MOLA at 400 random points inside the DTM: mean -3.6 m, std 24.9 m, so no vertical offset is applied. MOLA is 463 m/pixel and median-binned: it cannot represent terrain finer than that.","CTX part of horizons_ext is checked equal to skyline.horizons (imported, unchanged) at 24 candidates every run (max difference < 1e-6 deg).","A 20 m DTM cannot contain metre-scale rocks in the foreground; those rows of the skyline are part of the photo but not of the model.","Downloads this run: 0 images (cached ones not counted)."],"method":"Real Navcam frames (NASA/JPL-Caltech raw images), skyline traced and matched against CTX DTM + MOLA horizon; not simulated.","verdict":"FIX ACHIEVED (rule fixed before the held-out runs: FIX = error <= 500 m and uncertainty <= 1000 m; WEAK = error below the prior offset). Full method (panorama of 4 frames, 94% of azimuths scored, CTX + MOLA backdrop): error 51 m, uncertainty radius 50 m, min RMS 0.946 deg (prior offset 1757 m). Ablation errors (m): single/CTX 4153, single+MOLA 4153, panorama/CTX 51, full 51. At the waypoint itself the full-method RMS is 0.969 deg (residual median +0.26, 5-95% range -0.89 to +0.81 deg). One position, one run: not a statistical result."}